        "orario": "17:23",
        "timestamp": 1781018604,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 2026 World Cup participation conditional to US travel restrictions Americas Issued on: 09/06/2026 - 17:23 Modified: 09/06/2026 - 17:26 Traditionally, international sports competitions are seen as a way of overlooking division and differences, and disregarding geopolitics tension - which is the reason why North Korea competes in the Olympics for example. But this year's World Cup is proving an exception. Residents of countries placed on a US travel restriction list are finding their attendance at the World Cup is not garanteed. FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains. World Cup overshadowed by US travel restrictions and the war in Iran 09/06/2026 Americas Bolivia moves closer to state of emergency among large-scale protests 09/06/2026 Americas Trump booed at NBA Finals game in New York City 09/06/2026 Americas World Cup referee refused entry as US travel restrictions affect over 25% of participants 09/06/2026 Americas Trump booed at New York arena before NBA Finals game 09/06/2026 Americas Peru's polarising election: 'Neither candidate has strong majority' in Congress to enact reform 08/06/2026 Americas Inflation and FIFA price hikes dampen hope of World Cup boost to US economy 08/06/2026 Americas 08/06/2026 Americas Peruvians await results of elections for ninth president in a decade 08/06/2026 Americas"
